    "title": "Jokic triple-double, clutch in leading Nuggets past Booker, Suns",
    "text": "March 24, 2026Updated March 25, 2026, 7:26 a.m. MTThe Phoenix Suns continued their four-game homestand March 24 with a 125-123 loss to the Denver Nuggets before a sellout crowd of 17,071 at Mortgage Matchup Center.Nikola Jokic hit the game-winning midrange jumper with 11.8 seconds left.The three-time MVP posted a triple-double of 23 points, 17 rebounds and 17 assists as the Nuggets (45-28) swept the season series, 3-0, over the Suns (40-33).Devin Booker missed a 3 for the win with 1.9 seconds left. Booker paced the Suns with 22 points on 5-of-14 field goals and eight assists.Phoenix concludes its four-game homestand March 28 against the Utah Jazz (21-51).The Suns were without Dillon Brooks (left hand fracture), Mark Williams (left foot third metatarsal stress reaction), Haywood Highsmith (right knee injury management) and Amir Coffey (left ankle sprain).Peyton Watson (right hamstring injury management) sat out for the Nuggets.Nuggets close half strong, take leadThe Denver Nuggets ended the second quarter on a 21-8 run to take a 67-57 halftime lead over the Phoenix Suns.Three-time MVP Nikola Jokic is one assist shy of already racking up a triple-double as he has 15 points on 6-of-8 field goals, 11 rebounds and nine assists.Jalen Green leads the Suns with 14 points while Devin Booker has just seven points on only 2-of-4 shooting.Phoenix went from shooting 56% in the first quarter (6-of-15 from 3) to 27.3% in the second quarter (3-of-12 from 3).Allen, O'Neale available vs. NuggetsGrayson Allen (left knee injury management) and Royce O'Neale (left knee soreness) are set to return as both now available for Tuesday's game against the Denver Nuggets.Allen and O'Neale are welcomed returns as the Suns have been short-handed in recent games.O'Neale has missed Phoenix's last three games after playing in every game prior. He's set to start along with Collin Gillespie, Devin Booker, Jalen Green and Oso Ighodaro.Allen has sat out Phoenix's last four games. He's averaging a career-high 17.2 points a game.The Nuggets are starting Jamal Murray, Christian Braun, former Suns forward Cam Johnson, Aaron Gordon and three-time MVP Nikola Jokic.Suns injury update on Williams, DunnPhoenix Suns forward Ryan Dunn is a late scratch as he's been ruled out with right groin soreness.Dunn has scored 12 points in each of his last two games.Suns coach Jordan Ott said Mark Williams has yet to play 5-on-5, adding the team needs to see him play 5-on-5 before returning to action.Williams participated in an individual workout after Tuesday's morning shootaround. He's missed Phoenix's last 11 games. The Suns are 5-6 in those 11 games.Have opinions about the current state of the Suns? Reach Suns Insider Duane Rankin at dmrankin@gannett.com or contact him at 480-810-5518. Follow him on X, formerly Twitter, at @DuaneRankin.Support local journalism: Subscribe to azcentral.com today.",
